Description: Generic extension layer for the Proxmox VE web UI and API
 pve-ext provides three small, reusable seams so that adding an API module
 or a UI page to Proxmox VE never needs another one-off patch:
 .
  * API modules: PVE::API2::Ext scans /usr/share/perl5/PVE/API2/Ext/*.pm,
    requires each one and mounts it into the API root at the path it
    declares.
  * UI pages: pve-ext-loader.js fetches GET /api2/json/ext/pages and adds
    one tab per manifest (found under /usr/share/pve-ext/pages/*.json) to
    the matching LXC/QEMU/node/Datacenter config panel, as a native ExtJS
    panel.
  * Managed patches: pve-ext-patch applies, verifies, removes and reports
    on a set of dpkg-diverted file patches described by JSON manifests
    under /usr/share/pve-ext/patches/*.json.
 .
 pve-ext ships its own two-file manifest (the one-line hooks into
 index.html.tpl and PVE/API2.pm this whole layer depends on); other
 packages (e.g. pve-meta) depend on pve-ext and ship their own page
 manifests, API modules and/or patch manifests.
